{
  "id": "experience-sampling-method",
  "term": "experience-sampling method",
  "definition": "The experience-sampling method is a psychological research approach for gathering repeated measurements over time in everyday settings, producing intensive longitudinal data with strong real-world relevance. Its measurements are often taken at deliberately varied times across days rather than at equal intervals.",
